# Citation metadata for the Software Observatory.
#
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file, so a
# malformed one silently does nothing. Validate before committing:
#
#     pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate -i CITATION.cff
#
# `version`, `date-released` and the release DOI are added at release time —
# see the "Releasing" section of CONTRIBUTING.md. They are absent here rather
# than wrong: there is no tagged release yet, and a version number that does
# not correspond to a tag is worse than no version number.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Software Observatory catalog or framework, please cite it as below."
title: "Software Observatory: a catalog of epistemic sensors for software correctness"
abstract: >-
  A reference catalog of the signals engineering teams use to decide whether
  software is correct — tests, type checkers, mutation testing, canaries,
  formal methods, incident review and the rest — each rated on six
  dimensions: oracle strength, independence, scope, latency, actionability
  and predictive/reactive type. The catalog is organised into sensor families
  and mapped onto a confidence stack, so that a team can see which kinds of
  evidence it has, which it lacks, and which of its signals are correlated
  rather than independent.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Justin
    family-names: Abrahms
    website: "https://abrah.ms"
repository-code: "https://github.com/justinabrahms/software-observatory"
url: "https://softwareobservatory.com"
license:
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - software correctness
  - software testing
  - software quality
  - verification
  - observability
  - epistemology
  - taxonomy
